Nexus 0.13.4 exact cancellation after uncertain execution transport failure.
Upstream: d60ff582fde90c59726336c0dbdf3e8286e9df7a.
User approved 2026-10-15; N3-F1 continuation authorizes structured public outcome.
Retain at most 64 unknown identities. Never replay. Independent control uses no
execution slots. cancel_operation/cancel_active retain bool and exception behavior;
cancel_active is active-only again, so stale unknown IDs cannot starve it.
New cancel_operation_outcome reports cancelled/not_pending/failed, failure category,
per-handle attempt_sequence, ACK issuance cutoff and causal execution_stopped.
Only authoritative not_pending ISSUED AFTER a true ACK retires an unknown ID.
Delayed pre-ACK false and all failures retain it. Successful executions never
clear unrelated IDs. Active ACK state survives a later execution disconnect.
Close clears identity state. Server pending keys disappear after backend unlock;
exact cancellation prohibits queued cancelled operations from later executing.
Probes: scripts/nexus/probe_cancel_after_disconnect.py,
        scripts/nexus/probe_cancel_proof_ambiguity.py; tests/nexus_bridge/.
Removal: pinned upstream equivalent must pass probes and N0/N3 revalidation.
N3-F2: final connection cleanup cannot invalidate an already parsed outcome;
cleanup_failure and its exception type report teardown failure without credentials.
All ordinary final-close exceptions preserve the parsed authoritative outcome.
N9 packaging MUST carry this patch until then.

